      "writtenOn": "2025-02-14T17:34:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on the discussion, we are going to add the ip prefixes as local network prefix if \n1. For ipv6 link address have prefix length greater than zero\n2. For ipv4, we will check if link address is part of any static ipv4 local prefixes (link local, CGNAT, RFC1918)\n\nThis is consistent with route controller in netd. \nWe will always add multicast and broadcast address into local network prefixes. \n\nThe implication of this logic is we will only consider address as local if the route consider it local. If there is an address, for example in RFC1918 range that route does not consider local, we would not block it even if the application do not have required permission. \n\nfyi : @reubent@google.com",
      "parentUuid": "2b992a2f_0b3749cb",
