      "writtenOn": "2025-02-10T22:53:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This length is the length used by Trie for performing prefix matching. First 32 bits are for interface index matching (common for both ipv4 and v6). Then for v6 we are directly adding prefix length. For v4, we are storing v4 as v4-mapped-v6, for v4 we will have first 96 bits common ::ffff followed by ip address. So we are adding 96 (common length for v4-mapped-v6) + actual prefix length.",
